-- title:
--   Base change of mod-p two-cusp integral weight-two forms
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a non-zero natural number with $p \mid M$ but $p^{2} \nmid M$, let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and assume that every unit $u$ of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ whose image under the reduction map `ZMod.unitsMap` associated with the divisibility $(M/p) \mid M$ is trivial already lies in $H$; that is, $H$ contains the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$. Let $K$ be a field equipped with an algebra structure over $\mathbb{Z}/p$. Write $\Gamma_H(M)$ for [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ obtained as the image, under the inclusion of $\Gamma_0(M)$, of the preimage of $H$ under the homomorphism $\Gamma_0(M) \to (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ given by the lower-right entry mod $M$. Let [`CuspForm.IntTwoCuspForms M H p`](def/ModularCurve_XHDifferentialsModL.html#L374) be the quotient of the lattice [`CuspForm.twoCuspLattice M H 2 p A`](def/CuspForm_TwoCuspLattice.html#L86), an $A$-submodule of the weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma_H(M)$ taken over $A = (\bot : \text{Subring } \mathbb{C})$, the image of $\mathbb{Z}$ in $\mathbb{C}$, by the submodule $\mathfrak{p} \cdot \top$ with $\mathfrak{p}$ the ideal generated by $p$ in $A$; so it is the reduction of that lattice modulo $p$, regarded as a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-vector space. The conclusion asserts that $K \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}/p} \mathtt{IntTwoCuspForms}\, M\, H\, p$ is finite-dimensional over $K$ and that its $K$-dimension equals $\dim_{\mathbb{C}} \mathcal{S}_2(\Gamma_H(M))$, the $\mathbb{C}$-dimension of `CuspForm (CohCarrier.GammaH M H) 2`.
--
--   This is the dimension count attached to the integral structure on weight-two cusp forms: reducing the integral two-cusp lattice modulo $p$ and base changing to any field of characteristic $p$ preserves the dimension $\dim_{\mathbb{C}} \mathcal{S}_2(\Gamma_H(M))$. It feeds the comparison with regular differentials on the modular curve in [`ModularCurve.finrank_tensorProduct_intTwoCuspForms_eq_finrank_twoCompRegularDifferentials`](thm.html#ModularCurve.finrank_tensorProduct_intTwoCuspForms_eq_finrank_twoCompRegularDifferentials).
